# Missing Component Placeholder Pattern

## 🎯 Core Principle
**When a Figma design references a component that doesn't exist in `ft-design-system/ai`, ALWAYS use the MissingComponent placeholder.**

## ✅ Required Pattern

### When Component is Not Available

```typescript
import { MissingComponent } from '../components/MissingComponent';

// ✅ CORRECT - Use placeholder for missing components
<MissingComponent 
  name="ComponentName" 
  description="Brief description of the component from design"
/>

// ❌ WRONG - Don't build custom components
<div className="custom-component">...</div>

// ❌ WRONG - Don't use shadcn/ui or other libraries
import { CustomComponent } from '../ui/custom-component';
```

## 📦 Component Location
- Path: `/src/components/MissingComponent.tsx`
- Import: `import { MissingComponent } from '../components/MissingComponent';`

## 🎨 Usage Examples

### In Component Gallery
```typescript
{
  name: 'Missing Component Name',
  description: 'Description from Figma design',
  demo: (
    <MissingComponent 
      name="ComponentName"
      description="This component is shown in the design but not available in ft-design-system yet"
    />
  ),
  code: `// Component not available in ft-design-system/ai
<MissingComponent name="ComponentName" />`
}
```

### In Production Pages
```typescript
// If design requires a component not in the package
const ComponentFromDesign = () => {
  return (
    <MissingComponent
      name="Breadcrumb"
      description="Navigation breadcrumb component"
    />
  );
};
```

## 🚫 Forbidden Practices

### ❌ NEVER Do This:
```typescript
// Don't create custom implementations
const MyCustomButton = () => { /* ... */ };

// Don't use local ui/ components if npm version exists
import { Button } from '../ui/button';

// Don't build workarounds
const FakePlaceholder = () => <div>Coming soon</div>;
```

### ✅ ALWAYS Do This:
```typescript
// Use MissingComponent for unavailable components
import { MissingComponent } from '../components/MissingComponent';

<MissingComponent 
  name="ComponentName"
  description="From Figma design - not in npm package"
/>
```

## 📝 Props Interface

```typescript
interface MissingComponentProps {
  name: string;           // Component name from design
  description?: string;   // Optional: What the component should do
}
```

## 🎯 When to Use

1. **Design has a component** not in `ft-design-system/ai`
2. **Requested feature** needs a component that doesn't exist
3. **Figma mockup** shows a component unavailable in the package
4. **Migration scenario** where old component has no npm equivalent

## ✅ Benefits

- **Visual consistency**: Clear indication of missing components
- **No custom code**: Avoid building duplicate components
- **Easy tracking**: See what components are needed
- **Design feedback**: Designers can see what's missing in the package
- **Clean codebase**: No scattered placeholder implementations

## 🔍 Code Review Checklist

Before committing, verify:
- [ ] No custom component implementations for available npm components
- [ ] MissingComponent used for unavailable components
- [ ] No imports from `../ui/` folder (except MissingComponent)
- [ ] No duplicate component implementations
- [ ] All components from `ft-design-system/ai` or MissingComponent
